  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technology-enabled Open Schools for All (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Technology-enabled Open Schools for All project aims to support Egypt, Ethiopia and Ghana to design, pilot test, and scale up Technology-enabled Open School Systems that can connect school-based and home-based learning to ensure the continuity and quality of learning whether under normal or in crises situations. Building on the achievements of the first phase, a second phase is envisioned to continue and expand the digital transformation of education efforts. Phase II of the project spans three (3) years with a proposed budget of USD 2 Million and additional in-kind donation of equipment (valued at USD 1 Million) for three beneficiary countries: Brazil, Egypt and Thailand.</narrative>
  </description>
